      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE O'CONNOR: May I ask one preliminary question, Mr. Phillips? Do we have before us here any question at all about qualified immunity?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1423",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "02f8ab5f160eab6db4e25b290902e74771401c1240480f555d8d4aac0d607e91",
      "evidence_id": "ev-02f8ab5f160e-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PHILLIPS: Well, we do believe that a qualified immunity issue is bound up with the underlying merits."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1423",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "02f8ab5f160eab6db4e25b290902e74771401c1240480f555d8d4aac0d607e91",
      "evidence_id": "ev-02f8ab5f160e-0000-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "At issue in this case is the safety of police officers when they attempt to execute a search warrant in an inherently unsafe situation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1423",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "02f8ab5f160eab6db4e25b290902e74771401c1240480f555d8d4aac0d607e91",
      "evidence_id": "ev-02f8ab5f160e-0000-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SHANMUGAM: Thank you, Justice Stevens, and may it please the Court: When executing a search warrant to investigate a"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Shanmugam",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1423",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "02f8ab5f160eab6db4e25b290902e74771401c1240480f555d8d4aac0d607e91",
      "evidence_id": "ev-02f8ab5f160e-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It is our view that as a matter of law, the officers would have been entitled to prevail on the"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1423",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "02f8ab5f160eab6db4e25b290902e74771401c1240480f555d8d4aac0d607e91",
      "evidence_id": "ev-02f8ab5f160e-0001-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the officers did move for summary judgment. They also orally moved for judgment as a matter of law at the close of the evidence, and that motion was denied."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1423",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "02f8ab5f160eab6db4e25b290902e74771401c1240480f555d8d4aac0d607e91",
      "evidence_id": "ev-02f8ab5f160e-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Well -- well, has the -- the objection to the instruction been preserved here?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1423",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "02f8ab5f160eab6db4e25b290902e74771401c1240480f555d8d4aac0d607e91",
      "evidence_id": "ev-02f8ab5f160e-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Where -- where is that testimony?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1423",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "02f8ab5f160eab6db4e25b290902e74771401c1240480f555d8d4aac0d607e91",
      "evidence_id": "ev-02f8ab5f160e-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: If that's true, is it routine in -- I mean, here what sort of pushes the other way on this is this is a dangerous gang."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1423",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "02f8ab5f160eab6db4e25b290902e74771401c1240480f555d8d4aac0d607e91",
      "evidence_id": "ev-02f8ab5f160e-0002-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "court level, the -- the district court heard a rule 59."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1423",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "02f8ab5f160eab6db4e25b290902e74771401c1240480f555d8d4aac0d607e91",
      "evidence_id": "ev-02f8ab5f160e-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And with respect to handcuffing, I think our position on the handcuffing is that Summers, first of all, doesn't deal with handcuffing. And the other side has consistently tried to equate detention with restraint."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1423",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "02f8ab5f160eab6db4e25b290902e74771401c1240480f555d8d4aac0d607e91",
      "evidence_id": "ev-02f8ab5f160e-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Doesn't that just go to the point that it's not clearly established at least?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1423",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "02f8ab5f160eab6db4e25b290902e74771401c1240480f555d8d4aac0d607e91",
      "evidence_id": "ev-02f8ab5f160e-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE O'CONNOR: And what do we do if we think the Ninth Circuit was off base in -- in whether Mena could be questioned about her immigration status?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Carter G. Phillips (Petitioners)",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1423",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "02f8ab5f160eab6db4e25b290902e74771401c1240480f555d8d4aac0d607e91",
      "evidence_id": "ev-02f8ab5f160e-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "REBUTTAL ARGUMENT OF CARTER G. PHILLIPS ON BEHALF OF THE PETITIONERS\nMR. PHILLIPS: Thank you, Justice Stevens.\nI want to start with essentially the question that Justices Breyer and Kennedy raised, which is what do you do when you know that the Ninth Circuit is wrong, that the questioning here violated the Fourth Amendment, and what do you do when you know that the Ninth Circuit was wrong in saying that the officers have an affirmative duty in the middle of a Summers detention to make an assessment on an individualized basis as to the risks posed by any individual detainee. Those are rulings that I submit to you are plainly erroneous and warrant reversal on that"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1423",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "02f8ab5f160eab6db4e25b290902e74771401c1240480f555d8d4aac0d607e91",
      "evidence_id": "ev-02f8ab5f160e-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: So -- so do we have the tape here?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1423",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "02f8ab5f160eab6db4e25b290902e74771401c1240480f555d8d4aac0d607e91",
      "evidence_id": "ev-02f8ab5f160e-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: But there was no -- there was no objection to that question going to the jury, was the duration unreasonable."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1423",
